{
  "key": "hedging_stance_markers",
  "concept_slug": "hedging_stance_markers",
  "grounding_mode": "fallback_no_wiki",
  "title": "Hedging and Stance Markers in Norwegian",
  "cefr_level": "B2",
  "goal": "Use common Norwegian stance markers to express uncertainty, inference, shared assumptions, source doubt, opinion, and informal approximation.",
  "objectives": [
    {
      "id": "obj_uncertainty_inference",
      "statement": "Distinguish markers for uncertainty, inference, shared assumption, and reported or uncertain source.",
      "bloom_targets": [
        "understand"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obj_opinion_register",
      "statement": "Choose explicit opinion frames and informal approximation markers with suitable register.",
      "bloom_targets": [
        "understand"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obj_positioning",
      "statement": "Place stance markers naturally in Norwegian main clauses and avoid overloaded stacking.",
      "bloom_targets": [
        "understand"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_kind": "section",
      "id": "imported_section_000",
      "role": "orient",
      "objective_ids": [],
      "title": "What Stance Markers Do",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "A stance marker is a word or phrase that shows how strongly you stand behind what you say. In Norwegian, these small words often carry the difference between a guess, an inference, a shared assumption, a rumor, and a clearly framed opinion."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "rule",
          "statement": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Use one clear stance marker when it changes the meaning; avoid piling up several markers just to sound cautious."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Kanskje møtet blir flyttet til fredag."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Maybe the meeting will be moved to Friday."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Det blir nok lettere når vi har sett tallene."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "It will probably get easier once we have seen the numbers."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "These words do not all mean maybe. Some lower certainty, some present a reasonable conclusion, some invite agreement, and some signal that the source is indirect."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "element_kind": "section",
      "id": "imported_section_001",
      "role": "contrast",
      "objective_ids": [
        "obj_uncertainty_inference"
      ],
      "title": "Uncertainty, Inference, and Source",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "The safest way to learn these markers is by the kind of stance they express. Notice especially the difference between a plain possibility, a conclusion based on clues, and information you have heard but are not fully confirming yourself."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
